---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import VectorDbComparator from '../../components/VectorDbComparator.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Vector Database Cost Comparator"
  description="Compare estimated monthly cost across Pinecone, Weaviate, Qdrant, Zilliz, pgvector, and self-hosted options for your vector count."
>
  <VectorDbComparator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Vector DB pricing is not apples-to-apples</h2>
  <p>
    Managed vector databases price differently — some charge per vector,
    some have a flat base fee, and self-hosted options shift cost to server
    infrastructure instead. This makes a fair comparison hard without doing
    the math yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this comparator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Estimate your total vector count (in millions) — this usually equals your number of document chunks.</li>
    <li>Compare estimated monthly cost across providers.</li>
    <li>Factor in non-price considerations too: managed hosting saves engineering time even if it costs more.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Does self-hosted really cost less?</strong> Often yes on raw
    infrastructure, but it shifts cost to your own DevOps time for setup,
    scaling, and maintenance — factor that trade-off in, not just the dollar
    estimate.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
